---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { base } from "../lib/site";
---
<Layout
  title="Indiana"
  description="Things an IU student can do in Bloomington and across Indiana: Kirkwood, Lake Monroe, College Mall, and the drive home to central Indiana."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/indiana.html"
  current="indiana"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <p>College town · home weekends · the state in between</p>
      <h1>Indiana</h1>
      <p>
        IU sits in Bloomington. The rest of the state is still there when you need a lake, a mall day,
        or a kitchen that already knows how you take your rice.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <section aria-labelledby="origin-heading">
        <h2 id="origin-heading">Where I started</h2>
        <p>
          Central Indiana. Greenfield. A family Chinese restaurant in New Palestine ... Tuesday to Sunday,
          11am to 9pm, closed Mondays. That is the origin, not a cute extra. I learned to read a room
          from the dining room, then I learned to leave and come back.
        </p>
        <p>
          Indianapolis is the city mum drove toward. Libraries. Camps. Later, the airport shuttle when
          a semester goes further than Indiana. Go Express runs Bloomington to Indianapolis International.
          Students ride Bloomington Transit free with a valid IU ID.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="btown-heading">
        <h2 id="btown-heading">B-town, once you live here</h2>
        <ul class="direction-list">
          <li>
            <h3>Kirkwood Avenue</h3>
            <p>
              The strip from Indiana Avenue to College Avenue. Shops, food, and the nights everyone
              means when they say they are going out. Sample Gates looks down the street. Fountain Square
              sits on it. Buskirk-Chumley Theater too.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Fourth Street</h3>
            <p>
              International restaurants in a walkable row. Some students try to eat the whole street
              before they graduate. One or two good meals is enough for a first week.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Places I actually go</h3>
            <p>
              Herztl for hot chocolate in poppy cups when Indiana gets cold. Crumbl when the week needs
              a value system. College Mall for a nothing day that still counts. The Cade when you want
              pinball and a barcade. Friendly Beasts for a cider flight. Nick's English Hut if someone
              talks you into Sink the Biz ... float a Bismarck glass in a beer bucket, count to three.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Kirkwood after dark</h3>
            <p>
              If you want the longer insider map of bars, that already lives on
              <a href="https://matchaxmoxie.github.io/matchaxmoxie/b-town-bars.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">matchaxmoxie</a>.
              I am not cloning it here.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="outside-heading">
        <h2 id="outside-heading">Leave campus without leaving Indiana</h2>
        <ul class="direction-list">
          <li>
            <h3>Lake Monroe</h3>
            <p>
              About twenty minutes southeast of campus. Largest lake in Indiana if you do not count
              Lake Michigan. Swimming, boats, fishing, stargazing.               I have watched the sunset there with
              a crowd on the shore. Visit Bloomington still says rent a pontoon with friends, or skip
              rocks at Flat Rocks.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Griffy Lake Nature Preserve</h3>
            <p>
              About ten minutes from campus. Canoes, kayaks, paddleboards. No swimming. Short trails
              when you need trees more than a party.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Brown County</h3>
            <p>
              East of town. Forest, state park, the kind of drive people take in October because the
              colour actually shows up. I list it because students do it, not because I am selling a hike.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Switchyard Park and the B-Line</h3>
            <p>
              Largest developed city park. Food trucks, skate park, weekend events. The B-Line is the
              paved trail through town when you want to walk or bike without a destination speech.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Home weekends</h3>
            <p>
              Go home when you can. Your people miss you more than they say out loud. The restaurant,
              the drive, the kitchen ... that still counts as Indiana student life. You do not have to
              perform Bloomington every Saturday.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="more-heading">
        <h2 id="more-heading">More maps</h2>
        <ul class="proof-list">
          <li><a href="https://ois.iu.edu/get-involved/things-to-do/index.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">IU Office of International Services · things to do</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.visitbloomington.com/indiana-university/beyond-the-gates/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit Bloomington · beyond the gates</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.idsnews.com/article/2026/03/things-to-do-in-bloomington-48-hours" rel="noopener noreferrer">Indiana Daily Student · 48 hours in Bloomington</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <a href={`${base}spain.html`}>Spain, when the semester leaves the state</a>
          <a href={`${base}iu.html`}>Back to IU</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
